    "level": "junior",
    "tag": "backend",
    "description": "<div class=\"p-head\"><h1 class=\"p-title\">Absolute Value</h1><div class=\"p-meta\"><span class=\"pill lv-junior\">junior</span></div></div><h2>Context</h2>\n<p>A single <code>if</code> flips the sign of negatives \u2014 the simplest branch there is.</p>\n<h2>Task</h2>\n<p>Implement <code>Abs</code> in absif.go.</p>\n<p>Do <strong>not</strong> change the function signature or the tests.</p>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<pre class=\"md\"><code>\nAbs(-5) // =&gt; 5\nAbs(5)  // =&gt; 5\nAbs(0)  // =&gt; 0\n</code></pre>\n<details class=\"topics-foot\"><summary class=\"topics-lbl\">Topics <span class=\"topics-n\">3</span></summary><div class=\"tchips\"><span class=\"tchip\">Single if</span><span class=\"tchip\">Return value</span><span class=\"tchip\">Zero</span></div></details>",
    "education": "<h1>The single-branch if</h1>\n<h2>The idea</h2>\n<p>An <code>if</code> without <code>else</code> handles the exceptional case and falls through to the common return.</p>\n<h2>Why it matters</h2>\n<p>Guard clauses and early returns keep the happy path un-indented.</p>\n<h2>Watch out</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>math.MinInt</code> has no positive counterpart; ignore that edge for this junior task.</li>\n<li>No <code>else</code> is needed after a <code>return</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
