    "description": "<div class=\"p-head\"><h1 class=\"p-title\">Count Matching</h1><div class=\"p-meta\"><span class=\"pill lv-junior\">junior</span></div></div><h2>Context</h2>\n<p>Counting matches is a loop with a conditional increment \u2014 the smallest useful</p>\n<p>filter.</p>\n<h2>Task</h2>\n<p>Implement <code>CountEqual</code> in countword.go.</p>\n<p>Do <strong>not</strong> change the function signature or the tests.</p>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<pre class=\"md\"><code>\nCountEqual([]int{1,2,1,3,1}, 1) // =&gt; 3\nCountEqual(nil, 1)              // =&gt; 0\nCountEqual([]int{2,2}, 5)       // =&gt; 0\n</code></pre>\n<details class=\"topics-foot\"><summary class=\"topics-lbl\">Topics <span class=\"topics-n\">3</span></summary><div class=\"tchips\"><span class=\"tchip\">Loop + condition</span><span class=\"tchip\">Equality</span><span class=\"tchip\">Counter</span></div></details>",
    "education": "<h1>Conditional counting</h1>\n<h2>The idea</h2>\n<p>A running counter incremented under an <code>if</code> inside a loop is the basis of filters, histograms, and predicates.</p>\n<h2>Why it matters</h2>\n<p>It generalises to any predicate \u2014 the shape stays the same as the condition grows.</p>\n<h2>Watch out</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Return 0 for no matches, never -1 or a sentinel.</li>\n<li>A nil slice ranges zero times.</li>\n</ul>",
