    "title": "Curried Add3",
    "level": "middle",
    "tag": "backend",
    "description": "<div class=\"p-head\"><h1 class=\"p-title\">Curried Add3</h1><div class=\"p-meta\"><span class=\"pill lv-middle\">middle</span></div></div><h2>Context</h2>\n<p>Currying nests closures: each call captures one argument and returns a function</p>\n<p>waiting for the next.</p>\n<h2>Task</h2>\n<p>Implement <code>Add3</code> in curry.go.</p>\n<p>Do <strong>not</strong> change the function signature or the tests.</p>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<pre class=\"md\"><code>\nAdd3()(1)(2)(3) // =&gt; 6\nAdd3()(10)(0)(0) // =&gt; 10\n</code></pre>\n<details class=\"topics-foot\"><summary class=\"topics-lbl\">Topics <span class=\"topics-n\">3</span></summary><div class=\"tchips\"><span class=\"tchip\">Nested closures</span><span class=\"tchip\">Accumulated capture</span><span class=\"tchip\">Return function chain</span></div></details>",
    "education": "<h1>Currying with nested closures</h1>\n<h2>The idea</h2>\n<p>Each closure captures its argument and returns the next; the innermost sees the whole accumulated environment.</p>\n<h2>Why it matters</h2>\n<p>Currying underlies configurable builders and some functional APIs.</p>\n<h2>Watch out</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every inner closure captures its enclosing arguments by reference.</li>\n<li>The type signature nests exactly as the calls do.</li>\n</ul>",
