    "id": "01-language-basics/04-functions/middle/dropwhile",
    "title": "Drop While",
    "level": "middle",
    "tag": "backend",
    "description": "<div class=\"p-head\"><h1 class=\"p-title\">Drop While</h1><div class=\"p-meta\"><span class=\"pill lv-middle\">middle</span></div></div><h2>Context</h2>\n<p>DropWhile finds the first element failing the predicate and returns everything</p>\n<p>from there \u2014 the complement of TakeWhile.</p>\n<h2>Task</h2>\n<p>Implement <code>DropWhile</code> in dropwhile.go. Return a fresh slice (copy the tail).</p>\n<p>Do <strong>not</strong> change the function signature or the tests.</p>\n<h2>Examples</h2>\n<pre class=\"md\"><code>\nDropWhile([]int{1,2,-1,3}, pos) // =&gt; [-1 3]\nDropWhile([]int{1,2}, pos)      // =&gt; []\nDropWhile([]int{-1}, pos)       // =&gt; [-1]\n</code></pre>\n<details class=\"topics-foot\"><summary class=\"topics-lbl\">Topics <span class=\"topics-n\">3</span></summary><div class=\"tchips\"><span class=\"tchip\">Find boundary</span><span class=\"tchip\">Copy the tail</span><span class=\"tchip\">Complements TakeWhile</span></div></details>",
    "education": "<h1>Skipping a matching prefix</h1>\n<h2>The idea</h2>\n<p>DropWhile locates the first non-matching element and returns the remainder; copying the tail avoids sharing the caller's backing array.</p>\n<h2>Why it matters</h2>\n<p>Trimming leading whitespace/zeros/headers is DropWhile in disguise.</p>\n<h2>Watch out</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Returning <code>xs[i:]</code> directly would alias the caller's array; copy it.</li>\n<li>If everything matches, the result is empty.</li>\n</ul>",
    "starter": "// Package dropwhile \u2014 Gopher Workplace challenge.\npackage dropwhile\n\n// DropWhile skips the leading run where pred is true and returns the rest as a\n// new slice.\nfunc DropWhile(xs []int, pred func(int) bool) []int {\n\t// TODO(candidate): implement this from scratch so all tests pass.\n\tpanic(\"not implemented\")\n}\n",
